; Muskrat Ramble (Kid Ory, 1926), from a Real Book lead sheet (Veesh's): its key (Ab) and
; form. Each line ends with its bar numbers. Bars 1-32 the first strain's eight four times (the
; 1st and 3rd endings turn to C minor, the 2nd and 4th come home through Bbm), bars 33-48 the
; second strain (Bb7 Eb7 Ab, the trombone smear at its end).

